1. NEVER EDIT [rss.md](mdc:sources/rss.md) . NEVER EVER EDIT ANYTHING IN THE FOLDER sources/
2. Avoid Over-Engineering
    Minimize excessive error handlers, placeholders, and fallbacks.
    Keep solutions simple and avoid unnecessary abstraction.
3. Enforce Code Modularity
    Split files when they exceed 500 lines or contain distinct functional responsibilities (e.g., API calls, utilities, logic).
    Each module must be self-contained, properly exported, and imported where needed.The main file (e.g., app_client.py) should act as an orchestrator, managing imports and dependencies.
4. Structured File Header (≤10 lines)
    Each file must begin with a concise, structured header comment containing:
    Purpose: A brief summary of the file’s functionality.
    Exports: A list of exported functions/classes with:
        Name
        Parameters (strict TypeScript type annotations)
        Return Type
        Required Arguments
    Related Files:
        Dependencies & Interacting Modules (files below in the hierarchy).
        Parent Modules (files above in the hierarchy).
    Format: Use a consistent docstring or block comment.
    Keep Updated: Modify the header when the file’s role or dependencies change.
5. Maintain Single Responsibility Principle (SRP). 
   Each file, function, and class should have one clearly defined responsibility. Avoid overloading functions with multiple, unrelated tasks.
6. Error Handling Best Practices:
   Only catch expected errors; avoid excessive try/catch blocks. Log errors meaningfully, including the function name and relevant data.Propagate critical errors instead of suppressing them silently.